text: |-
  Grass
  @DewyGrassBlades • 1h
  Their own article admits the FBI was complicit from day one so why on
  earth would they not release everything now instead of giving the FBI tim
  to bury the truth? I'll review all the evidence with an open mind, but this
  stinks of corruption from the start!
  Former FBI Special Agent Kyle Seraphin
  realized Friday that he was doing surveillance
  next door to the woman now suspected of
  being the Jan. 6 pipe bomber.
  "The FBI put us one door away from the pipe
  bomber within days of January 6, and we were
  deliberately pulled away for no logical or
  logically investigative reason," Seraphin told
  Blaze News Friday. "And everything about
  that tells me that they were involved in a
  cover-up and have been since day one.
